---
import "../styles/docs.css";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { articleHref, docArticles } from "../data/docs-catalog";
import { gallerySvg } from "../data/hero-slides";

const agentDocs = docArticles.filter((article) => article.group === "Agents");

const chart = gallerySvg("line");
const description =
  "Agents write one JSON spec, validate it, repair the safe mistakes, and render SVG. llms.txt is at /llms.txt.";
---

<Base tone="light" title="Agents" description={description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="agents-page-title">
      <p class="kicker">Agents</p>
      <h1 id="agents-page-title">The spec is the interface.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An agent writes JSON. <code>validate()</code> returns every CK code in one pass. <code>repair()</code> applies the safe JSON Patch and does not call a model. <code>render()</code> returns SVG. No other library in the eval has a schema and a repair function.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/validate">Validate and repair</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/docs/charts/line">Line chart</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="loop-title">
      <h2 id="loop-title">The loop</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Write</h3>
          <p>
            <code>version</code> is <code>"1"</code>. <code>data</code> is an array of rows. <code>a11y.alt</code> is one
            sentence and is required. Gauge, kpi, and progress-ring put the number in <code>metric</code>.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Validate</h3>
          <p>
            <code>validate()</code> checks the schema and the data. <code>CK1001</code> is invalid JSON.{' '}
            <code>CK1004</code> is a missing required field such as <code>a11y</code>.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Repair</h3>
          <p>
            <code>repair()</code> returns a spec and the patch it applied. It does not invent data. A missing or unknown
            type is reported first.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Render</h3>
          <p>
            Core charts come from <code>@chartkitdev/core/all</code>. Histogram through rose, and the planning charts,
            come from <code>@chartkitdev/core/extra</code>. <code>render()</code> does not validate and does not throw.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="measured-title">
      <h2 id="measured-title">What the eval measured</h2>
      <p>
        With the docs in the prompt, a measured run wrote a valid chart on 42 of 42 tasks. <code>repair()</code> took a
        no-docs run from 21/42 to 42/42 with no model call. Round 6, 2026-10-16. Not re-run since. Losses stay on the
        benchmark page.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://chartkit.dev/benchmarks#agents">Benchmarks, losses included</a>
      </p>
      <div class="agent-chart" set:html={chart}></div>
      <p class="note">The line above is the same example spec the docs try-it paints, rendered here with core.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="prompt-title">
      <h2 id="prompt-title">What to give the model</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> is the short index: the rules, the repair loop, and one spec per chart type.{' '}
          <a href="/llms-full.txt">llms-full.txt</a> is the long file.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/schema/v1.json">schema/v1.json</a> is the JSON Schema.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/docs/llms-txt">llms.txt notes</a> and <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP</a>.{' '}
          <code>@chartkitdev/mcp</code> is not on npm yet. The server speaks stdio. <code>render_chart</code> is the tool
          that calls Cloud.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="agent-docs-title">
      <h2 id="agent-docs-title">In the docs</h2>
      <p>The same short list as the docs Agents group. Chart pages stay in the docs nav.</p>
      <ul>
        {agentDocs.map((article) => (
          <li>
            <a href={articleHref(article)}>{article.title}</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
